  was not distributed with this file, You can obtain one
  at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.

  This file is covered by the PaskalCPP Runtime Exception
  (RUNTIME-EXCEPTION.md).
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  raven.pcpp - the raven unit: `import raven;` builds user interfaces with
  Raven (https://github.com/oscar-soirey/Raven), a GUI library in C11:
  widgets, layout panels, themes, XML-described windows, text input, menus,
  dialogs. A self-describing vendor module: it owns every include path,
  library path and link library it needs, per official target. The library
  is libraven.a (one per target), built by PaskalCPP-Libs' build-raven.cmd
  from Raven's own CMake project (static; examples, tests, tools and web
  pages off), shipped under Raven's Apache-2.0 license with its NOTICE and
  the licenses of the components it bundles (stb, Roboto, Roboto Mono,
  tweetnacl) in res\libs\vendor\raven. On Windows it links winhttp user32
  gdi32 shell32 comdlg32 ole32; on Linux X11 pthread m dl. Its Vulkan
  renderer opens the Vulkan loader at run time: nothing links it.

  Inside a raylib program Raven is used through raven_raylib (raylib keeps
  the window, the loop, audio and the game's drawing; Raven draws its
  widgets in the raylib frame). On its own, the API is Raven's C API as it
  ships, called straight from PaskalCPP:
  - Setup: Rinit(R_BACKEND_VULKAN) opens Raven with its own OS windows;
    Rinit_ex(address of LDesc) takes an RInitDesc (backend, app_name,
    headless = true for no OS window, disable_render_thread). R_BACKEND_NULL
    renders nothing (headless runs and tests). Rshutdown() ends it.
  - Windows and widgets: Rwindow_create(title, width, height,
    R_WINDOW_DEFAULT) gives a window's Rid; Rwidget_create(R_WIDGET_VBOX)
    and the kind constructors (Rlabel_create, Rbutton_create, ...) give
    widgets; Rwidget_add_child(parent, child) places a child and returns
    it; Rwindow_set_content(window, root) sets what a window shows.
  - Each frame: Rdraw_frame() processes the pending events, runs the
    posted tasks and timers, then lays out and paints the windows that
    changed (false once Rquit was called or the last window is closed); a
    headless window takes its input through Rwindow_inject_mouse_move /
    _mouse_button / _mouse_wheel / _key / _text.
  - Callbacks are C functions: `routine clink OnClicked(AButton: Rid;
    AUserData: ptr)` passed by its bare name, e.g. to
    Rbutton_set_clicked_callback(button, OnClicked, nil).
  - Errors: Rerror_set_callback(handler) reports Raven's errors with their
    code, severity and detail (Rerror_to_string / Rseverity_to_string).
  - Files: every load (XML windows, themes, fonts, textures, Rfile_read)
    looks in Raven's memory files first (Rfile_register_memory), then opens
    the path with the C runtime, which HookIO reaches: a zip such as
    bin\assets.zip loads with Raven's own calls, through an io:// prefix
    (RegisterIOSource(CreateZipIOSource(archive, password)) + "/entry") or
    with the zip as the thread's path source (SetIOThreadPathSource) and the
    entry's own name. An XML window's images and fonts are named relative to
    it and come from the same place.
==============================================================================*/

module unit raven;

// Self-describing vendor module: it owns every path it needs.

@addincludepath "$P:res/libs/vendor/raven/include";

@ifdef TARGET_X86_64_WINDOWS_GNU
  @addlibrarypath "$P:res/libs/vendor/raven/lib/x86_64-windows-gnu";
@elseif TARGET_X86_64_LINUX_GNU
  @addlibrarypath "$P:res/libs/vendor/linux64/lib";
  @addlibrarypath "$P:res/libs/vendor/raven/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu";
@else
  @message error "raven: unsupported target";
@endif

@linklibrary "raven";

@ifdef TARGET_X86_64_WINDOWS_GNU
  @linklibrary "winhttp";
  @linklibrary "user32";
  @linklibrary "gdi32";
  @linklibrary "shell32";
  @linklibrary "comdlg32";
  @linklibrary "ole32";
@elseif TARGET_X86_64_LINUX_GNU
  @linklibrary "X11";
  @linklibrary "pthread";
  @linklibrary "m";
  @linklibrary "dl";
@endif

// The header goes to this unit's header, so every importer sees Raven's API
cpp header;

#include "Raven.h"

end.
